<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ sees net debt at 23.4 pct of GDP in 1997/98.</title>
<headline>NZ sees net debt at 23.4 pct of GDP in 1997/98.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand's Treasury in the Budget Policy Statement released on Tuesday projected net public debt at 23.4 percent of GDP in 1997/98.</p>
<p>In the December Economic and Fiscal Update the comparable projection was 23.6 percent of GDP.</p>
<p>Actual latest figures show the ratio was 29.1 pct at December 31.</p>
<p>The ratio is projected in the Budget Policy Statement to be 21.0 percent of GDP in 1998/99 and 17.8 percent in 1999/2000.</p>
<p>The government's net worth is projected to be NZ$9.3 billion in 1997/98.</p>
</text>
